 "missing_frames": [],
 "arc": "A two-beat side-step-tap, danced square to camera with a constant knee bounce. The cycle opens with the weight already settled over the character-right foot on the balls of both feet, the bounce carrying downward into the beat. Frames 1-3 are the first tap: the character-left foot lifts and crosses behind the character-right, touches, and the weight rocks back to centre as both forearms float up to chest height. Keep the lift small — this is a tap, not a step out.\n\nFrames 4-6 are the transfer: weight passes through centre with the legs nearly straight at the top of the bounce, forearms dropping back to waist height. That straightening is the anticipation for the second tap, so let the knees rebound rather than hold.\n\nFrames 7-11 mirror the first half onto the other side — weight on the character-left foot, character-right foot lifts and crosses behind, the character-left shoulder rides up and the head turns character-right to follow the step. The character-left forearm swings across in front of the torso and stays there through the hold. Frames 12-15 are the recovery: weight returns to centre then settles back over the character-right foot with both feet down, head squaring up again, so the last frame lands on the same planted, bounced-down pose frame 0 opens on. The seam is one natural bounce — do not add a settle.",
